-- title:
--   Ramification of the Igusa level field over X₀(M') in characteristic q
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`); write $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Inside $\kappa((T))$ consider the intermediate fields $E_0 =$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the $\kappa$-subfield generated by the two $j$-series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $M'$, and $E =$ `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the $q$-expansion function field attached to the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ for $H = \ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\bigr)$. Assume as hypotheses the inclusion $E_0 \le E$ and that the corresponding inclusion ring homomorphism is integral; give $E$ the induced $E_0$-algebra structure. Let $w$ be a place of $E$ over $\kappa$ (a valuation subring of $E$ containing $\kappa$, proper, and a principal ideal ring), and let $v$ be its restriction along the inclusion, i.e. the place of $E_0$ whose valuation subring is the preimage of that of $w$. Then the ramification index $e(w) = \inf\{n > 0 : n = \mathrm{ord}_w(f) \text{ for some } f \in E_0,\ f \ne 0\}$ satisfies: $e(w) = (q-1)/2$ (natural subtraction and division) whenever $v$ lies in `ssPlaces q M' κ`, the set of places of $E_0$ satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace`; and $e(w) = \max\bigl(1, \mathrm{placeWidth}\,M'\,v\bigr)$ otherwise, where `placeWidth` is the quotient of the $j$-width of $v$ evaluated at the geometric $j$-generator by the $j$-ramification of $v$.
--
--   This is the local ramification computation for the Igusa-type covering of the reduced modular curve in characteristic $q$: the extension is totally ramified of degree $(q-1)/2$ above the supersingular places of $X_0(M')_\kappa$ and has index $\max(1,\mathrm{width})$ elsewhere, so that it is unramified away from the supersingular locus and the elliptic points. It feeds the uniqueness of the place above a supersingular place and the Riemann–Hurwitz genus computation for the level-$H$ function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_ramificationIndex_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH_modularFunctionFieldC_eq_of_liesOverPrime.lean

